  "steps": [
    "All five: Put each protein in its own slow cooker with every ingredient in its group except the Greek yogurt and the cornstarch slurry. Whisk the liquids and seasonings together first and pour them over the meat.",
    "All five: Cook the chicken on LOW 6-8 hr or HIGH 3-4 hr, until it shreds easily and reads at least 165°F. Cook the beef on LOW 8 hr, until it pulls apart with a fork.",
    "Lemon herb chicken: Shred the chicken in the juices. Let it stand 5 min off heat, then stir in the Greek yogurt so it does not curdle.",
    "Honey garlic beef: Lift out the beef, shred it with two forks, discard any large pieces of fat, and toss it back in the sauce.",
    "Buffalo chicken chili: Lift out the chicken, shred it, and stir it back into the beans and tomatoes.",
    "Sesame ginger chicken: Shred the chicken. For a thicker sauce, whisk the cornstarch into the 2 tbsp water, stir it into the cooker, and cook on HIGH 15-20 min until glossy.",
    "Tuscan chicken: Shred the chicken, let it stand 5 min off heat, then stir in the Greek yogurt.",
    "All five: Taste and adjust the seasoning, then portion each into 6 containers. Refrigerate up to 4 days."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Each protein makes 6 servings. Add a carb and a vegetable to build meals.",
    "Chicken breasts are done well before 8 hours on LOW; most published slow cooker versions call for 4-6 hr on LOW, so start checking for 165°F at 4 hours."
  ],
